WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
Put a small positive
charge near another charge.

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.600
It feels a force, with
nothing touching it.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.940
The region around a charge
is an electric field.

4
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.960
It is there even when
nothing is placed in it.

5
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.810
To picture it, we draw field lines: each
shows the direction of the force on a

6
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.460
positive charge.

7
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.960
But those lines are just drawn on paper.

8
00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.370
How can their spacing tell
you how strong a force is?

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.180
In this mission, you'll sketch
field patterns for single charges,

10
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.540
pairs and parallel plates.

11
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.010
Then you'll add the fields of two charges,

12
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:37.130
and find where between
them the field is zero.

13
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.690
Your mission: explain how the spacing
of field lines can tell you how strong a

14
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.680
force is.
